{
  "_notes": [
    "Scores: 4 bytes on 4-byte centres from 0x021109E4. Stride 8 yields 0 and 0xFFFFFFFF.",
    "current_player and current_ball were resolved by the joint pair test, not by reading bytes.",
    "Independent 1->2->3 detection could not do it here: 0x00037315 topped the sweep at 680 hits",
    "against a next-best of 130 and is not a counter at all -- 0x00037314 holds a rising 32-bit",
    "little-endian value and 0x37315 is its second byte, reading 1, 2, 3 as it crosses 256, 512 and",
    "768. Searching a static exit dump for an adjacent (player=4, ball=3) pair gave 40 candidates.",
    "Requiring the two bytes to move together -- the player wrapping to 1 in the same sample the ball",
    "steps up -- returned exactly one hit for the whole game, and it is one of those 40.",
    "Free Play derived by aligning this game's adjustment array against a game where it was measured",
    "(32/35 agreement), which places it at index 33, 0x02102110. The value there reads 1 on a cabinet",
    "in free play and its check byte validates. Machine adjustments are 8-byte records from",
    "0x02102008: a 32-bit little-endian value, then a byte holding 0xFF minus the sum of the value's",
    "four bytes. All 88 records here satisfy that. Writing this field requires updating its check",
    "byte, or the game discards the change on reload.",
    "game_over measured from a 925-frame recording of live memory across two games, sampled about",
    "five times a second. The byte at 0x000381AE takes exactly two values over the whole recording:",
    "19 while a game is running and 1 in attract and after game over. Decoding it as bool with",
    "mask 0x12 and invert gives the correct state in all 925 frames, with transitions at game start,",
    "at game over about six seconds after the last score change (the bonus and match sequence), and",
    "at the start of the next game.",
    "mask 0x12 is the two bits that differ between the two observed values rather than a guess at",
    "which one carries the meaning; only those two values were ever seen, so a narrower mask would",
    "be asserting more than was measured.",
    "It is not adjacent to current_ball -- it sits 0x32 bytes past it, outside the window a",
    "neighbourhood search first covered.",
    "ball_count, max_credits, credits and tilted come from a 1,070-frame recording of live memory",
    "spanning an operator-menu session and a full game. Balls Per Game and Maximum Credits were set",
    "to distinctive values (5 and 9) so the changed records named themselves: adjustment index 30",
    "went 3 to 5 and index 32 went 30 to 9, both check bytes moving with them.",
    "credits at 0x0211100C -- the same address st_162h measured -- rose 0,1,2 as six coins were",
    "inserted at three coins a credit, and fell to 1 when the game started.",
    "The byte at 0x000381AE is a status bitfield, not a plain flag: it read 0x01 in attract, 0x13",
    "during play, and 0x15 for exactly the eight samples between the tilt and the end of the tilted",
    "ball -- during which player 1's score sat frozen at 40,360, the same corroboration that",
    "confirmed st_162h's tilt flag. So tilted is bit 0x04 of that byte, and game_over's mask 0x12",
    "decode stays correct in all 1,070 frames of this recording on top of the 925 that set it.",
    "2026-11: game_over is mask 0xFE inverted and tilted the value 0x15 (mask 0x1F) on 0x000381AE:",
    "mask 0x12 took the mode value 4D for game over, and bit 0x04 is set in 4D and in 5F, read on a",
    "cabinet while tilt warnings came in.",
    "2026-11: Master Volume and the A.1 (64) and A.2 (24) adjustments added from the ROM image",
    "(README, 'Adjustments from the ROM').",
    "Confirmed on a cabinet 2026-11-13 (ALP4K; two players, tilt on P1 ball 1): 930,050 / 890,720,",
    "the records and the status byte matched the DMD."
  ],
